00:06:13,492 --> 00:06:43,276
Protocol and design detail: What 1364-2001 Adds Over 1995 (1). ANSI-style port declarations: Direction and type (and size) in the port list always @*: Implicit sensitivity for combinational logic (no manual list) generate: Conditional and loop-based instantiation and logic signed: Signed arithmetic and signed nets/variables From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

28
00:06:43,626 --> 00:07:15,402
Protocol and design detail: What 1364-2001 Adds Over 1995 (2). Multi-dimensional arrays: e.g. reg [7:0] mem [0:255] localparam: Named constants that cannot be overridden ANSI-style task/function: Input/output in the header Other: File I/O improvements, $signed/$unsigned, attribute syntax, etc. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

29
00:07:15,752 --> 00:07:37,688
Protocol and design detail: What 1364-2001 Still Does Not Include. No SystemVerilog: no logic, always_comb/always_ff, interfaces, packages, classes No type parameters or interfaces (those are 1800) From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

30
00:07:38,038 --> 00:08:03,022
Protocol and design detail: ANSI-C Style Ports. input wire: Default for input; can omit wire (e.g. input [7:0] a). output reg: Required when the output is driven in always/initial. output wire: When the output is driven only by assign or submodule. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

31
00:08:03,372 --> 00:08:20,412
Protocol and design detail: Comparison: 1995 vs 2001 Port Style. Same behavior; 2001 is more concise and keeps port and type in one place. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

32
00:08:20,762 --> 00:08:44,378
Protocol and design detail: always @* Syntax. **@* (or @(*)**): Sensitive to every signal read in the block (RHS and conditions). Use for combinational logic only; do not use for sequential (use always @(posedge clk)). From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

33
00:08:44,728 --> 00:09:07,552
Protocol and design detail: When to Use @* vs Explicit List. Prefer @*: For combinational blocks; fewer errors, easier to maintain. Explicit list: When targeting strict 1995 compatibility or when a tool does not support @*. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

34
00:09:07,902 --> 00:09:28,230
Protocol and design detail: generate / endgenerate. genvar: Loop variable for generate loops; not a runtime variable. generate for: Replicates logic/instances; index must be constant at elaboration. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

35
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:42,188
Protocol and design detail: Conditional Generate. generate if / else: Choose one of several implementations at elaboration. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

36
00:09:42,538 --> 00:10:02,362
Protocol and design detail: signed Wire and reg. signed: Affects arithmetic and comparison in expressions involving that net/reg. Unsigned (default): No sign extension; values 0 to 2^N-1. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

37
00:10:02,712 --> 00:10:25,608
Protocol and design detail: Declaration and Usage. Packed (left): [7:0] — contiguous bits, can be used as a single vector. Unpacked (right): [0:255] — array of elements; select with one index at a time in 2001. From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

38
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:57,686
Protocol and design detail: Task (2001 ANSI). automatic: Optional; gives automatic storage (re-entrant). Useful for recursive or concurrent calls. input/output in header: Cleaner than 1995 style; avoids duplicate declarations. Note: In 1364-2001 use output reg (not output logic; logic is SystemVerilog). From MODULE2 Topics Covered — protocol/design depth.

39
00:10:58,036 --> 00:11:05,836
